    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d51-a1-a3">

                <pb facs="0094" n="70" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg70"/>

                <head>Mr. F. W. Seward to Mr.
                        Savage.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-04-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 14, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi>Your despatch No. 136 has been received, in
                    which you call attention to the case of Don José Agustin Arguelles. I am
                    instructed to inform you that if the captain general will send to New York a
                    suitable officer, steps will, if possible, be taken to place in his charge the
                    above named individual for the purpose indicated in your despatch. You will
                    immediately communicate the purport of this instruction, in confidence, to the
                    captain general.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. W. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas Savage</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Vice-Consul General of the United States, Havana.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
